A||N||10||Monkeyman||What kind of tape should I use?||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-18-2001||05:04 AM||||I just bought a wing that won't be here until the middle of next week.  I just sold the wing that's currently on my car.  The buyer of my wing was gracious enough to let me hold on to it for a little while but I have to ship it on Monday.  Here's the problem.  It's supposed to rain early next week.  I don't have a garage to store my Fiero and it's a daily driver so I'll need to temporarily tape up my wing holes in my decklid.<P>What kind of tape can I use that will peel back off without either lifting the paint or leaving a nasty residue?  This tape will be on there for at least a couple of days, maybe longer depending on whether or not FedEx is on time (took them an extra week the last time I had something shipped through them).<P>Any suggestions?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||5
Z||000001||operator64||10-18-2001||06:18 AM||||   Just fill the bolt holes with some extra bolts you have laying around, use a piece of bicycle innertube on top as a " washer " to keep the water out or you could use some silicone on the inside.<BR>     Hope this works for ya.<BR>      Operator||||reg||1
Z||000002||AusFiero||10-18-2001||07:53 AM||||Good quality masking tape is pretty water resilliant MM and comes off no worries. I have 3M tape blocking the holes in my MR2 decklid while I have the rear spoiler off awaiting fitment of the ricer wing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000003||Sage||10-18-2001||08:38 AM||||Clear silicon.  Seals and peels!<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||10-18-2001||09:44 AM||||small hunk of modeling clay(oil based kind not playdoh)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cozmo||10-18-2001||10:10 AM||||Plastic License plate bolts work great. Less than $2 at Wally World.<P>BobC||||reg||1
Z||000006||Butter||10-18-2001||10:20 AM||||Chewin' gum & duct tape, Hmmmm<BR>Let me count the ways.||||reg||12
Z||000007||NEPTUNE||10-18-2001||11:57 AM||||Use duct tape on the INSIDE, unless it has been painted.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe Torma||10-18-2001||12:14 PM||||I used masking tape...it got wet and now I can't get it off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||10-18-2001||01:09 PM||||If you do use masking tape, use the blue kind.It doesn't bond on like the white tape. ||||reg||1
